# Hermes smoke testing follow-up: graft nudge delivery is silent-on-success
# Reported by Cipher-311d (Hermes smoke-testing coordinator) while smoke-testing
# AI3133-HERMES-NUDGE-ROUTING-GAP fix (PR #688, commit 9baa734b,
# branch testing/hermes-smoke-testing off integrate/phase-ai-31-33)
# Non-blocking to PR #688; recorded as a follow-up observability gap.

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3133-GRAFT-SUCCESS-OBSERVABILITY-GAP>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3133-GRAFT-SUCCESS-OBSERVABILITY-GAP" ;
  triage:title "Daemon graft nudge delivery chain emits no log/event on success" ;
  triage:description "Cipher-311d reported that during smoke-testing of PR #688 (AI3133-HERMES-NUDGE-ROUTING-GAP fix), skillrx (the Hermes gateway operator) had no daemon-side log or event to confirm a successful graft nudge delivery -- only the smoke harness's own round-trip proof. Independently verified: the daemon chain DaemonRequestDispatcher -> DaemonPostSendHookEmitter -> DaemonGraftPostSendPort is silent-on-success by design. DaemonPostSendHookEmitter::emit_post_send (crates/atm-daemon/src/post_send_emitter.rs:30-46), for the Graft target arm (lines 40-43), calls graft_port.deliver_post_send() and returns Ok(PostSendEmissionPath::GraftPort) with no tracing call on the success path. DaemonGraftPostSendPort::deliver_post_send (crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs:86-113) resolves the roster member, computes the graft receiver record path, and calls deliver_post_send_to_graft_receiver (runtime_health.rs:116-134), which on GraftPostSendResponse::Delivered simply returns Ok(()) -- no tracing::info!/debug! anywhere in this path. By contrast, every failure branch in this file (roster lookup miss, missing graft root, transport error) is wrapped in a descriptive AtmError, and DaemonRequestDispatcher itself uses tracing::warn! extensively elsewhere (e.g. runtime_health.rs:247,278,287,330,347,393,412,436,510) but not on the graft post-send success path. There is no info/debug log or projection event emitted anywhere in this chain when a graft nudge is delivered successfully." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "HERMES" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-28T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI-S3133-HERMES-SMOKE ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-28T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-GRAFT-SUCCESS-OBSERVABILITY-GAP/graft-post-send-port> ,
    <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-GRAFT-SUCCESS-OBSERVABILITY-GAP/post-send-hook-emitter> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "testing/hermes-smoke-testing" ;
  triage:promoteTo "integrate/phase-ai-31-33" ;
  triage:rootCause "The graft post-send delivery chain (DaemonRequestDispatcher -> DaemonPostSendHookEmitter -> DaemonGraftPostSendPort) treats successful delivery as a no-op: deliver_post_send_to_graft_receiver returns Ok(()) on GraftPostSendResponse::Delivered without emitting any tracing event, and emit_post_send's Graft match arm likewise emits nothing on the Ok path. Only failure paths produce diagnostics (AtmError construction plus scattered tracing::warn! calls elsewhere in the dispatcher). Recommended fix: emit a tracing::info! (or a runtime_health_observability event, consistent with the existing SubsystemObservability pattern used for peer_duplicate_write_skipped) on the graft success path, including message_id, recipient, sink=\"graft\", and outcome=\"delivered\", so operators (e.g. skillrx at the Hermes gateway) have a daemon-side confirmation signal independent of the smoke harness's own round-trip proof. Scope should be limited to the two touch points identified: DaemonGraftPostSendPort::deliver_post_send / deliver_post_send_to_graft_receiver (runtime_health.rs) and, optionally, DaemonPostSendHookEmitter::emit_post_send's Graft arm (post_send_emitter.rs) if a hook-level event is preferred over a port-level one." ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-GRAFT-SUCCESS-OBSERVABILITY-GAP/graft-post-send-port>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs" ;
  triage:line 131 ;
  triage:snippet "GraftPostSendResponse::Delivered => Ok(())," ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:branch "testing/hermes-smoke-testing" ;
  triage:headSha "9baa734b" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/hermes-smoke-testing-graft-observability> ;
  triage:evidence "Cipher-311d smoke-testing report on PR #688: skillrx had no daemon-side log/event to confirm successful graft delivery, only the smoke harness's own round-trip proof. Code inspection confirms DaemonGraftPostSendPort::deliver_post_send (runtime_health.rs:86-113) and deliver_post_send_to_graft_receiver (runtime_health.rs:116-134) return Ok(()) on success with zero tracing calls; only error branches are instrumented." .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI3133-GRAFT-SUCCESS-OBSERVABILITY-GAP/post-send-hook-emitter>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
